Add the public headers for the Slingshot Link (SL) driver, the 400 Gb/s
link layer used by the second generation Cassini NIC.  SL is an
independent driver from SBL; a NIC uses one or the other depending on
its generation, so the two do not share code.

As for SBL, every header of the driver, including those private to one
layer, is added here so that each later patch compiles on its own.

The Kconfig and Makefile hookup for this driver is deliberately the
last patch of the driver group, so that every earlier patch adds
sources without changing what the tree builds.

